{
 "concept": "Silhouette: one tall red-timber refinery tower is the landmark, stacked on a wide machine hall base so it reads as vertical stacking. Its pagoda-style steep hip roof and a tall spire sit well above everything else, at least 1.8x the next volume. Two side workshops step down in height and roof type: a wide process hall with a sawtooth roof and furnace chimney, and a lower lab wing with a hip roof, joined by a short bridge across a gap to a small crane/gantry annex. Materials: dark deepslate base and plinth (60), red-stained timber look from crimson planks and stripped crimson stems for piers and walls (30), copper trim, cut copper cornices and cyan glass plus glow for ember light (10). Features: chimneys on the furnace hall, gears on the workshop face, pipe runs on the process hall, a spire on the tower, a platform for the terraced base, and a bridge across the yard to the crane annex. Interiors stay big: wide 11-13 high halls, and the height goes into the tower.",
